title: Stateless iteration-loop primitive shipped (v6.7.0)
summary: 'Implemented Orchestrator.runIterationLoop — the stateless re-review/iterate-with-same-role primitive from decision TD-2026-06-09-522. Born from the not-chat SendMessage/persistent-subagent debate: the team (Arky/Builder/Loid) reframed it — the re-context tax only bites in intra-specialist loops and we lacked an iteration primitive, so build that statelessly with no experimental-flag dependency. Three guardrails in code: typed iteration-verdict block for convergence (ping-pong honors only the reviewer''s approval), required maxRounds with structured unresolved exits (never a silent pass), and belief-revision-gated promotion to a NEW durable self-revision channel (iteration-revisions.jsonl → self_reflection journal) kept separate from human-verdict provenance. Arky''s spec corrected the original advisor contract in 4 places (provenance pollution chief among them). Loid+Reviewer pass caught two real bugs pre-commit: ping-pong fixer-self-approval and unconditional transferable:true. 12 unit tests; 210 core + 286 mcp tests green. Per user feedback, design consultation routed through Arky (our Architect) instead of the generic advisor tool so learnings compound.'
